; C13b  Winning 42 p. 49 (W42-p049-a, W42-p049-b)
; Rule, in our words: a setter holding exactly two tiles of a suit, one of them
; count, follows the bidder's double of that suit with the other one, and keeps
; the count tile guarded for the bidder's off.
; Python gate (pour_setter gate_c13b): a setter, the bidder led a non-trump
; double, the mover holds exactly two followers, one count; the book's tile is
; the non-count one.
; How this encoding differs: none from the gate. With three or more followers
; it does not fire; C8 (c08-no-count-on-the-double.silas) does. The book plays
; the same protection on trump doubles (Hand 33, p. 111), which the gate
; excludes.

(include book)

(policy c13b-protect-the-count
  (fallback lowest-legal)
  (rule follow-with-the-guard
    (select answer)
    (guard
      (query (roles (chair me) (domino doubled) (domino guard) (domino counted))
        (out guard)
        (pattern
          (viewer me)
          (setter me)
          (bidder-led doubled)
          (double doubled)
          (not (trump-tile doubled))
          (follower guard)
          (count guard 0)
          (follower counted)
          (count-tile counted)
          (none (roles (domino third))
            (follower third)
            (not (tile third guard))
            (not (tile third counted))))))))
